      "writtenOn": "2020-10-29T16:33:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it can because this code is only run for a module if it is the correct apex variant of this module. So, if the boot jars include \"com.android.art:core-libart\" then this will only match for the \"com.android.art\" variant of \"core-libart\". It cannot match \"com.android.art.test\" because that is a different variant.\n\nOne slight complication is that there appears to be some optimization of apex variants to merge variants for different apexes that are actually identical. e.g. That might mean (not sure if it does) that there is only one APEX variant for \"core-libart\" that covers \"com.android.art\", \"com.android.art.debug\" and \"com.android.art.test\". The code InApex(string) method handles that.\n\nI will add a check to detect duplicates.",
